# FastAPI Project Conventions

## Stack
- Language: Python 3.11+
- Framework: FastAPI
- Package manager: Poetry (or pip with requirements.txt)
- Runtime: Python 3.11+
- Code style: Black (formatting), Ruff (linting)
- Type checking: mypy (strict mode)

## Project Layout
```
app/
  main.py                # FastAPI app, lifespan, middleware
  routers/               # APIRouter with @router.post, @router.get
  services/              # Business logic, calls repository
  repositories/          # SQLAlchemy queries, async sessions
  models/                # SQLAlchemy ORM models
  schemas/               # Pydantic models (request/response)
  core/
    config.py            # Settings via pydantic-settings
    security.py          # JWT auth, password hashing
    database.py          # AsyncEngine, get_db dependency
alembic/
  versions/              # Migration files
  env.py
tests/
  unit/                  # Unit tests (mocked DB)
  integration/           # Real DB, isolated transactions
  contract/              # Validates responses vs OpenAPI spec
openapi.yaml             # Source of truth
pyproject.toml           # Poetry dependencies
```

## Agentic Workflow Rules

1. **contracts.md is the single source of truth.** Always read `contracts.md` before making changes to any API endpoint, schema, or data model. Update it whenever contracts or DB schema change.
2. **openapi.yaml is the spec — never modify it to match bad behaviour.** If implementation doesn't match the spec, fix the implementation.
3. **Build one endpoint group per session.** Scope each agent session to one route group (e.g. `/orders`). Small scope = clean diffs, easier reviews.
4. **Commit at checkpoints.** Commit after: spec creation, schema/migration verification, each completed endpoint group, passing test suite.

## Forbidden Patterns

- No raw SQL strings — use SQLAlchemy queries only
- No business logic in routers — delegate to services
- No secrets or credentials in code — use environment variables via pydantic-settings
- No `Any` types — use proper type hints everywhere
- No sync SQLAlchemy — always use AsyncSession
- No sync HTTP clients — use httpx.AsyncClient, never requests
- No skipping linter errors — run ruff and mypy, fix all errors before proceeding
